fell in love with Ruth  they started a relationship and in a  tragic twist her trying to help him by  getting him released from a mental  hospital set things in motion for his  downfall  I'm not gonna retell the whole story of  season 3 here the important thing for  this video is how his  death might affect everyone else going  forward I should say that I do believe  he's dead  I know we're trained to be skeptical if  we don't see the person actually die or  we don't see the body as proof but I  also believe that the story is best if  he is actually dead I don't think it  would be a good twist if they pull him  out later on and be like oh yeah  remember all that stuff that happened at  the end of season 3 it was all just the  fool you don't worry Ben is fine so yes  I do think he's dead I don't think  there's any chance he's gonna come back  it turns out to be a very difficult  situation for everyone that's involved  after arguing was Wendy about what  really happened  Ruth decided to leave the birds we saw  that Jonah was definitely struggling  with this and I thought the interesting  thing that came out of it was in the  immediate aftermath Marty was very  supportive to Wendy so the next big  question for me then would be will Marty  and Wendy work together as a team again  as tragic as Ben's death was will it  turn out to be the thing that brings  Marty and Wendy back together with Ruth  gone Marty will need someone to take her  place Wendy would be the most likely  candidate but it would require them to  work together in a way that they didn't  in season three and what about the rest  of the family who will all be coming to  terms with Ben's death first let's talk  about what the show is going to do with  Charlotte in season two she had this  close friendship with Wyatt and went to  a lawyer to try to get herself  emancipated in season three there was  very little mention of either of those  things and when we saw her she was  either working at the office or hanging  out with Helen's daughter Erin right  before Marty and Wendy left for Mexico  they gave her the keys to buddy's  mausoleum to coordinate the laundering  through the gamblers  well she get more involved with the  family business and are they just  dropping her friendship with Wyatt from  the story completely Jonah is an even  bigger question mark since we saw how  angry he was about Ben's death he first  turned his anger towards Helen but when  he went to visit her and threatened her  she made it clear that his parents  signed off on the murder we watched him  put the pieces together of their  involvement when he saw Ben's ashes  firing a shotgun blast through a window  in their home in a fit of rage he's  always been an odd character and he  doesn't really have any friends where  are they gonna take his story from here  and what about baby Zeke he was only a  part of their family for a short period  of time but none of the birds were happy  to see him end up with Darlene and  there's good reason for that  Wendy seemed determined to get him out  of that situation but her initial plan  to make Darlene look unfit didn't work  out things got crazy so fast with been  Helen and the cartel that there really  wasn't time to go back to it so going  into season four we have to wonder if  they will still try to get Zeke back  another character who I wonder about is  Rachel after everything that happened at  the blue cat and with her working for  agent petty  she did manage to make it out at least  as far as we know when we last saw her  Marty gave her a plane ticket to Miami  where he arranged the stay in the rehab  that he had prepaid for and he gave her  a down payment offering to buy her out  of the blue cat while all of this feels  like a fine way to write her out of the  story  the chemistry she developed with Marty  would make a return of the character  carry some weight have we seen the last  of Rachel and I guess by extension have  we seen the last of tuck we could ask  the same thing about two of the new  characters in this season Frank jr. and  Aaron Frank jr. wasn't my favorite  character he was annoying he was just  sort of there to cause problem in the  end Darlene took care of him she shot  off his manhood and that could be the  last we see of him and even though she  went to talk to his father and kind of  make him an offer we never saw him  explicitly agree to anything so there's  definitely a possibility that Frank jr.  might cause some problems going forward  Aaron is somewhat more interesting just  because of the stakes we would imagine  that she would go back to Chicago and  live with her father but I don't think  we could say for sure that the cartel  would be fine with her being out there  in the world she did give Jonah his  first kiss so he may stay in touch with  her and in that case if something were  to happen to her that might really push  him even further over the edge another  big question I have at the end of season  three is  what's gonna happen with the FBI we saw  them arrest Sam at the end of season  three Marty wasn't really that concerned  about that considering how nervous he  was about doing what he was doing it's a  little bit hard to believe that he won't  cave once they get him in an  interrogation room beyond that Maya  definitely knows that Marty and the  birds are connected to the Navarro  cartel to this point she hasn't been  able to prove it  Marty's been trying to get some leverage  against her which seems nearly  impossible because we know that she  isn't crooked we know that she's still  gonna be at the casino the warrant has  been extended so it'll be interesting to  see where things go  agent Evans should still be around as  well we last saw him working with Helen  who won't be returning so everything on  the FBI side of things is completely up  in the air one of the big character  ships in season three was Wyatt he now  seems to be all in on a relationship  with Darlene and I wonder what a future  for those two will turn out like Darlene  seems to be concerned was starting a  legacy getting the heroin business back  in full swing and creating a new crime  family that consists of locals with the  lang mores it makes you wonder if three  might play a more important role in  future seasons he was sort of sidelined  in season three it makes you wonder if  Darlene and Ruth would be able to work  together  Darlene hates the birds and I don't  think we should ever overlook that when  we think about her future plans for the  time being Ruth is also pretty firmly in  the anti bird camp but these are two  strong personalities we saw that Ruth is  absolutely capable in the work that she  did ver Marty but I'm not sure we could  say that Darlene will put up with the  same things that Marty would this whole  new alliance it just seems like there's  so many things that can go wrong with it  and it seems really unlikely that all of  these major players will make it out of  season four alive I also wonder if  someone will take Helens place Helen  essentially took the place of Dell who  was the go-between between Navarro and  the birds in the past the way things are  now it seems like Marty and Wendy are on  top of the food chain so would there  even be somebody else that what  come to take their place that makes me  wonder about Nelson who worked  side-by-side with Helen for so long well  he now works side-by-side with the birds  and if so how is someone like Jonah  gonna think about that also Ruth is  smart enough to know that she can't  really go after Nelson but his presence  should be particularly unsettling for  her he killed her father and her lover  so so seeing him around that could cause  issues but then again they might not  really cross paths  there's so many questions but I think  these are the biggest ones that are on  my mind right now  I'm really interested to see how Jonah  develops they always hinted that he was  sort of a strange character and Ben's  death really brought out the anger in  him at the end of the season at the same  time he's been somewhat accepting of  their situation he looks up to Marty at  least and he showed an interest in what  they actually do seeing the Lange Moors  on the same side as Darlene I mean  there's so much that could happen there  where things go also depends on how many  seasons we think there might be I know  that they've said in the past that they  thought about five it all depends on  where they land regardless of how many  seasons they do I think at this point we  can say that it's going to be crazy  wherever they go in season for the  cartel won't change they're not gonna  let up and that means that the pressure  will always be there so I'm gonna leave  it there those are my big questions tell  me in the comments what yours are what  you're hoping to see in season four what  are your favorite theories please like  this video if you enjoyed it please  subscribe to my channel if you haven't  already I'm thinking about doing some  more ozark videos over the next couple  weeks thanks for watching I will talk to  you soon
 

